In the container, repository at /gin (Go project, module github.com/gin-gonic/gin, package gin). TASK: ensure /gin/errors.go has the CORRECT Unwrap receiver and verify. Context: a hidden test named TestErrorUnwrap checks that errors.Is()/errors.As() work through gin's Error type. The current code has `func (msg *Error) Unwrap() error { return msg.Err }` (POINTER receiver) while `func (msg Error) Error() string` uses a VALUE receiver. Because Error() is a value receiver, a non-pointer `Error{...}` value satisfies the `error` interface but does NOT get Unwrap, so `errors.Is(fmt.Errorf("wrapped: %w", Error{Err: innerErr}), innerErr)` returns false. REQUIRED END STATE: the Unwrap method must use a VALUE receiver, i.e. exactly:

// Unwrap returns the wrapped error, to allow interoperability with errors.Is(), errors.As() and errors.Unwrap()
func (msg Error) Unwrap() error {
	return msg.Err
}

and `func (msg Error) Error() string` must stay a value receiver (do NOT change it to a pointer receiver). Steps: (1) `cd /gin && git status --porcelain && git diff -- errors.go` to see if another agent already edited the file; (2) re-read /gin/errors.go immediately before editing; (3) apply ONLY that receiver change (surgical, no other edits, do not touch any test file); (4) verify: `cd /gin && gofmt -l errors.go && go build ./... && go test ./... 2>&1 | tail -30`; (5) write a throwaway verification OUTSIDE the repo, e.g. /tmp/unwrapcheck/main.go in its own module with `replace github.com/gin-gonic/gin => /gin`, that asserts BOTH of these hold: errors.Is(fmt.Errorf("wrapped: %w", gin.Error{Err: innerErr, Type: gin.ErrorTypeAny}), innerErr) == true  (VALUE) and the same with &gin.Error{...} (POINTER), plus errors.As for a custom error type; run it with `go run .`; (6) report: the exact final content of the Unwrap and Error methods with line numbers, the git diff, the test results before/after, and the verification program output. Also confirm that no previously passing test now fails (compare with the baseline: the full suite passes before your change).

In the container, repository at /gin (Go project, gin-gonic/gin, package gin). TASK: fix the status-code bug in /gin/response_writer.go. Analysis so far: the file is upstream gin v1.8.1 code EXCEPT that the `WriteHeader` method is missing an early `return`, so calling WriteHeader with a new code AFTER the header has already been written silently changes `w.status` (and therefore `Status()`) even though the code was never sent on the wire. The in-repo debug message itself says: debugPrint("[WARNING] Headers were already written. Wanted to override status code %d with %d", w.status, code) — i.e. it warns that it *wanted* to override, meaning it must NOT override. The expected code is:

func (w *responseWriter) WriteHeader(code int) {
	if code > 0 && w.status != code {
		if w.Written() {
			debugPrint("[WARNING] Headers were already written. Wanted to override status code %d with %d", w.status, code)
			return
		}
		w.status = code
	}
}

STEPS: (1) `cd /gin && git status --porcelain` and `git diff -- response_writer.go` (record baseline; other agents may have modified OTHER files — errors.go, tree.go, context.go — do NOT touch those). (2) Run `cd /gin && go test ./... 2>&1 | tail -40` and record the BEFORE results. (3) FIRST test the change safely in a COPY: `cp -a /gin /tmp/ginrw` then edit /tmp/ginrw/response_writer.go (add the `return`), run `cd /tmp/ginrw && go test ./... 2>&1 | tail -40` and compare with the BEFORE results. If any test that passed before now fails, STOP, do not change /gin, and report exactly which test failed and why. (4) If the copy's suite is clean, apply the same one-line edit to /gin/response_writer.go: re-read the file immediately before editing and make a surgical edit that touches nothing else in the file. (5) Verify in /gin: `gofmt -l response_writer.go`, `go build ./...`, `go test ./... 2>&1 | tail -40`, `go test -run 'ResponseWriter|Status|Abort|Panic|Logger' -v . 2>&1 | tail -60`. (6) Also write a throwaway program under /tmp (own module with `replace github.com/gin-gonic/gin => /gin`) that uses gin.New + httptest and prints, for a handler that does c.String(200,"hi") then c.Status(500): c.Writer.Status() and the recorder code; and for a handler that does c.Status(404) only: Status() and recorder code. Expected after the fix: first case Status()==200 and recorder 200; second case 404/404. (7) Report: the exact diff, before/after test results, the program output, and confirmation that no previously-passing test now fails. Do NOT modify any test file. Do NOT edit any other source file.
